      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors its founder, Matthew Thomas Stallings, a farmer‑merchant who moved from Harrisburg and helped shape the early community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stallings%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A gristmill established in the late 1700s laid the groundwork for the Stevens Mill area that later became central to Stallings’ early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stallings%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Stallings’ first industry was a sawmill opened by Mark Conder, which attracted workers and spurred the growth of a small settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stallings%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s early economy relied on lumber shipped by rail to Charlotte and other destinations, linking Stallings to the regional rail network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
